    "solution": "Catch the lower west grip and climb. Wait for the lower circuit to move below the first crossing, then walljump and dash up-right through the airborne refill to the east grip. Immediately dash upward along that wall through its crystal, then climb toward the next transfer. Hold briefly while the next patrol moves down; the reference route departs with about eighteen stamina remaining. Walljump left and dash up-left through the middle crystal to the fresh upper west face. Climb, then cut right to light the nearby tally and open the upper pier. Dash upward beside the wall and jump right into a wallbounce; collect the last airborne crystal, then dash up-right through the final patrol stroke to the receiving gallery. No floor resets the three-grip phrase.",
    "nearestExisting": "B59 supplies the one-grip/refill/next-grip lesson; F59 supplies the wallbounce-to-aerial-refill finish. This taller synthesis alternates three individually spent faces, uses an early wall boost to set the later stamina budget, and changes the upper pier with a blade cut before the final timed departure. It is a continuous shaft, not three safe floor resets.",
    "novelty": "Learn one continuous climb rhythm across three consumed grips, finite stamina, refills and returning patrols.",
